{
 "schema": 1,
 "_about": {
  "what": "The 10 broken parts of the new tutorial (G:/nasa app/broken_parts/BPnn_*.blend), exported to Godot by tools/blender/broken_parts/export_broken_parts.py + build_broken_parts_data.py. Contract: docs/revisions/BROKEN_PARTS_BRIEF.md.",
  "coordinates": "Godot world metres. Each glb is already placed (Blender map_matrix_world, Blender (x, y, z) -> Godot (x, z, -y)): instance it at the origin (identity transform) under the world.",
  "glb": "Root node = the glb's file name (BP01..BP10). Its children are the nodes listed in `nodes` (name, kind, parent). Materials are the shared res://materials/colony/<role>.tres (assets/broken_parts/broken_part_post_import.gd), render layers come from ColonyZones like the map's pieces, and every mesh has the `dust` instance uniform set.",
  "kind": "model = the broken object itself (fades/shrinks out at the fix); effect = vapour / water spray / puddle / spilled liquid / glass shards / dust / alarm lamps, stopped at the same moment; seal = BP08 door seal piece, a child of its leaf.",
  "hide_objects": "data/colony_manifest.json object names hidden while broken; hide_nodes = the same as Godot node names under the Colony instance of scenes/world/colony_world.tscn (the glTF import turns 'a.001' into 'a_001').",
  "bounds": "AABB of every node of the glb (Godot). model_bounds = only the model nodes (the sparkle burst area).",
  "spot": "the brief's Godot spot of the part; station_id = the repair station in data/stations_repairs.json that opens its mini-game.",
  "special": "'' normal swap; 'door_901' = see `door` (T12); 'dust' = see `dust` (T11).",
  "door_leaves": "T12: the nodes that slide with each leaf of door 901 (L slides -x, R +x).",
  "door": "T12: the exit-tunnel inner door (EnvironmentCollision door 901). Its intact leaves are not map objects: EnvironmentCollision cuts them out of SFX_tunnel_inside (environment.glb) at run time as the Node3D/MeshInstance3D nodes named in hide_env_nodes (siblings of SFX_tunnel_inside). While broken, hide those and show the glb's leaves; to slide a broken leaf, move its node along slide_axis by slide_m * open_amount from its rest transform (same as DoorController: left -1.75 m, right +1.75 m on Godot x). The seal nodes are children of their leaf and move with it. alarm/vapour are effects; light = the red alarm glow of the source render (optional, add an OmniLight3D there if wanted).",
  "dust": "T11: the hangar objects keep their meshes; while broken set the instance uniform `dust` (colony_surface.gdshader, instance uniform float dust) of every MeshInstance3D of the Hangar area to broken_value, and back to its fixed value afterwards (the manifest object's dust: 0.55 for the Hangar, hb_rover 1.0). broken_value 3.0 is the source blend's value; the shader clamps dust x surface mask to 0..1, so 3.0 = upward faces fully covered. The dust mesh hg_dust__broken (drifts, floor layer, boot prints) is cut into a 12 x 2 grid of patch nodes hg_dust__broken_r<row>c<col> (dust_nodes; rows along Godot z, columns along x over dust_region, the same grid HangarDust.area_of uses), shown only while broken, hidden area by area."
 },
